<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title><?= esc($pageTitle) ?> · Sun Son Solar</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="<?= base_url('css/style.css') ?>"><link rel="stylesheet" href="<?= base_url('css/solar-app.css') ?>"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"></head><body class="legalPage"><header class="siteHeader"><a class="brand" href="<?= site_url('/?view=storefront') ?>"><img src="<?= base_url('css/images/logo.png') ?>" alt=""><span>sun son<span class="brandAccent">solar</span><small>POWER YOUR EVERY DAY</small></span></a><a class="navCta" href="<?= site_url('/?mode=login') ?>">Customer & staff sign in ↗</a></header><main class="legalContent"><a class="legalBack" href="<?= site_url('/?view=storefront') ?>">← Back to Sun Son Solar</a><span class="sectionKicker">SUN SON SOLAR · <?= strtoupper(esc($pageType)) ?></span><h1><?= esc($pageTitle) ?></h1><p class="legalLead">Last updated <?= date('F Y') ?> · This page describes the class-project demonstration site.</p><?php if ($pageType === 'privacy'): ?><h2>Information you provide</h2><p>When you create a customer account, the site stores the profile details you submit. If you request a solar assessment or support, it stores the bill estimate, roof details, request text, and the status and notes needed to follow up in your portal.</p><h2>How the demo uses it</h2><p>The information is used to display your profile and route your quote and service requests to authorized Sun Son Solar staff accounts. Passwords are stored as one-way password hashes. Never enter real sensitive, financial, or utility account information into this classroom demo.</p><h2>Access and retention</h2><p>Administrators can view customer records and manage account access. This demo does not provide a self-service data export or account deletion feature. A production service should publish verified contact details, a retention schedule, and a process for access, correction, and deletion requests.</p><?php else: ?><h2>Solar estimates and packages</h2><p>Package descriptions, prices, and estimated savings on this demonstration site are illustrative planning examples. They are not a final offer, engineering assessment, savings guarantee, or contract. System design and pricing depend on a site assessment, roof and electrical conditions, equipment selection, utility requirements, and a written proposal.</p><h2>Account use</h2><p>Customers are responsible for keeping their sign-in details private and for submitting accurate information. Employees use accounts provisioned by an administrator and must replace their initial password on first sign-in.</p><h2>Requests and project updates</h2><p>Submitting a quote or service request starts a conversation; it does not confirm a purchase, installation date, warranty, or response-time guarantee. Project stages and notes in the portal are operational updates.</p><h2>Service readiness</h2><p>This is a classroom project. Before use with real customers, Sun Son Solar should review these terms, provide verified business and support contact details, and confirm applicable consumer, privacy, electrical, and utility requirements.</p><?php endif ?><a class="primaryCta" href="<?= site_url('register') ?>">Create a customer account <span>↗</span></a></main><footer class="legalFooter">© <?= date('Y') ?> Sun Son Solar · <a href="<?= site_url('terms') ?>">Terms</a> · <a href="<?= site_url('privacy') ?>">Privacy</a></footer></body></html>
